dle the case.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: 400 schools closed as student protests continue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89d7a2c963c62092162c8a29f152a212aa3872536aa9f92744ed5d9458343542</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T17:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-400-schools-closed-as-student-protests-continue/a-79512732--ddc0e5e9d750.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-400-schools-closed-as-student-protests-continue/a-79512732?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police have made around 2,000 arrests and dozens of people have been injured as student protests spread across France. Ministers have called for a "day of dialogue" but students have called for further strike action.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>FlyDubai 'hero' pilot speaks for first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21aa5dbc5a4019afdb27b6da8f28451fc6d2afd3a1b62411ce28ae3a45b78e54</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:50:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T17:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flydubai-hero-pilot-speaks-for-first-time/a-79524500--a2a707eed39f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flydubai-hero-pilot-speaks-for-first-time/a-79524500?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's Prime Minister Narendra Modi spoke with Captain Smit Machchhar via video call. Meanwhile, authorities in the UAE and Israel said an investigation is making progress.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain's parliament rejects housing bill as protests continue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81fe142d144f8974f3523b627ab75c21a28d1a8a201afff4a6b9e424604ef62d</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:50:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-s-parliament-rejects-housing-bill-as-protests-continue/a-79522683--f3b2b2f36991.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-s-parliament-rejects-housing-bill-as-protests-continue/a-79522683?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's minority government suffered defeat in parliament as it tried to push through a pair of emergency measures aimed at making housing more affordable. A pensioner's eviction and protests led to the bid.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>"NAZA": Israeli military issues statement on film</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a658f83854655697f69f0e670851be610f801fced6714836f64f5d0f71dc738a</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:50:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/naza-israeli-military-issues-statement-on-film/a-79520483--c29108607d5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/naza-israeli-military-issues-statement-on-film/a-79520483?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The award-winning documentary "NAZA" continues to spark controversy in Israel. The Israeli military has now published a multi-page statement calling the film's portrayal "distorted."</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's top court allows Arab parties to run in election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dfaf60eb991f95ebb16c82493448d1e048f7e832bff8c08cf8f7d25f95b24bbb</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:50:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-s-top-court-allows-arab-parties-to-run-in-election/a-79519184--8c7a89ad00e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-s-top-court-allows-arab-parties-to-run-in-election/a-79519184?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ruling overturns a move by the Central Elections Committee to ban four parties. The conservative Muslim Ra'am party could serve as the kingmaker following the next elections.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran accused of blocking SIM cards, digital access to silence dissent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:547022603fc5c3be41acee848c73d00ebb6974b9e9596007e4b8ae6a8141edba</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-accused-of-blocking-sim-cards-digital-access-to-silence-dissent/a-79522440--050f09779478.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-accused-of-blocking-sim-cards-digital-access-to-silence-dissent/a-79522440?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has spoken with several Iranians who say their SIM cards, bank access and online accounts were blocked until they deleted critical content or pledged to stop activism.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Europe to release diesel reserves after Trump request</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e590136fb40d3998f2dfc229ac3e06f9d711d8de11c5e9797421c8e027cd7c77</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:50:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-to-release-diesel-reserves-after-trump-request/a-79522810--4bf471a88a09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-to-release-diesel-reserves-after-trump-request/a-79522810?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US leader asked European countries to release some of their diesel reserves to ease the rising prices. The issue has damaged Trump's popularity back home.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Franz Reindl elected new IIHF president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dd06f2cd9db615e1bb6127708c2a9e530f92ed1c98a2ee1673023c76e8fcc10</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-franz-reindl-elected-new-iihf-president/a-79521799--24f017ae08ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-franz-reindl-elected-new-iihf-president/a-79521799?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Franz Reindl has been elected president of ice hockey's world governing body. The former forward was a member of West Germany's Olympic bronze medal-winning team.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Argentina launches cash-for-citizenship scheme</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e512576a78bf4048d46692d209c4a5866786b3fddd7b6619d58013044688d16b</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/argentina-launches-cash-for-citizenship-scheme/a-79520708--9871152522e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/argentina-launches-cash-for-citizenship-scheme/a-79520708?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investors seeking the fastest but most costly route to Argentine citizenship can choose between a non-refundable gift of $350,000, or buying a government bond for $800,000, if they think that will pay off in the end.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can there be solar for all, everywhere by 2030?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae500770859784833cb6e2d415a491969d0740369fd5201675b53f46f8c3f14d</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-there-be-solar-for-all-everywhere-by-2030/a-79517056--2e42319aeceb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-there-be-solar-for-all-everywhere-by-2030/a-79517056?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prominent climate leaders have called on governments, businesses, institutions and the public to make a push for solar power before the decade is out, repowering the world with cheap, clean energy. Is that possible?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>North and South Korea trade accusations over landmines that injured three soldiers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:294f2dcca33b1e14e0d52d12d705f0f8b2c02dffb020bdd114dc275bc6062082</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-and-south-korea-trade-accusations-over-landmines-that-injured-three-soldiers/a-79503854--57b9ec347358.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-and-south-korea-trade-accusations-over-landmines-that-injured-three-soldiers/a-79503854?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A mine blast that injured three South Korean soldiers has renewed scrutiny of North Korea's actions along the border and raised questions about its strategic goals.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City Premier League charges: What do they mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2b4be4694f34226de860e5298969eeceba03fafccb9eb0f4eb6d4155c944660</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638--5f423a99075f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since being bought by the UAE in 2008, Manchester City have become one of the world's most successful football clubs. A raft of serious financial charges threatens to undermine this and bring chaos to the Premier League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Half of Europe witnessed record heat stress this summer — EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a5ccfb19427d746989d61ec6a2b0cce5fa43c378fa4dc148ea5f5c4f8743f00</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/half-of-europe-witnessed-record-heat-stress-this-summer-eu/a-79514799--b11552623347.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/half-of-europe-witnessed-record-heat-stress-this-summer-eu/a-79514799?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's climate monitor said this summer was third-warmest for the continent on record. European rivers also registered their lowest average flows since records began in 1992.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>This island in Kiribati could be the key to solve the Amelia Earhart mystery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c309450134deb9dc9b7675b3d67416514aaf55ac3d5390336c4a70245b6b840e</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-island-in-kiribati-could-be-the-key-to-solve-the-amelia-earhart-mystery/a-79517455--5be17a2d6029.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-island-in-kiribati-could-be-the-key-to-solve-the-amelia-earhart-mystery/a-79517455?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly 90 years after US aviator Amelia Earhart vanished over the Pacific, a new expedition to the remote island of Nikumaroro hopes a lagoon anomaly could finally reveal the fate of her missing aircraft.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>ARD-Deutschlandtrend survey: Germans unite in frustration over the government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:388ac166405e4b7f6342d2a115ad735c8d7f953a60705ac1bfd6f1647eb13cf1</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ard-deutschlandtrend-survey-germans-unite-in-frustration-over-the-government/a-79515172--1741214668c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ard-deutschlandtrend-survey-germans-unite-in-frustration-over-the-government/a-79515172?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On the 36th anniversary of reunification, Germans are dissatisfied with the country's political leaders. They don't believe they'll be able to handle the challenges posed by AI, Russia and Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Reform row raises fears for Merz's coalition</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f575dd11270d6b985842a242c1527dd211ef44faa8cb918f143b5f9bc65ec1f3</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-reform-row-raises-fears-for-merz-s-coalition/live-79512757--9a7ffc72b3eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-reform-row-raises-fears-for-merz-s-coalition/live-79512757?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's conservatives are dialing up the pressure on their center-left partners ahead of crunch talks next week. Meanwhile, Volkswagen's latest cost-cutting push has triggered a furious response. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Kyiv bridges shut after fatal Russian drone assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:046c7bed72ab2be6e2ce1ed15ab0cb2382e96ced53665553e2d5c264297908c5</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-kyiv-bridges-shut-after-fatal-russian-drone-assault/a-79510950--d4ee88fd9446.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-kyiv-bridges-shut-after-fatal-russian-drone-assault/a-79510950?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The latest Russian attacks killed at least one person and severely disrupted traffic in the Ukrainian capital. Several bridges over the Dnipro River connect western and eastern Kyiv.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Who could bring the warring sides to the negotiation table?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f8afc65f2e70e6770442dc6ece640bff28a22809fe059a09b5cda51cd3d8a89</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-who-could-bring-the-warring-sides-to-the-negotiation-table/a-79475529--2936c02781db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-who-could-bring-the-warring-sides-to-the-negotiation-table/a-79475529?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia might be facing its most complex armed conflict in contemporary times. The fragile 2022 peace deal has collapsed. International mediators have failed. How will the country return to normal?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan: first new F-16V fighters arrive amid China threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25eb1840d65232df31ed6de5f581b9e8ecf3264fc60c057513acc23735af1f47</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T07:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/taiwan-first-new-f-16v-fighters-arrive-amid-china-threat/a-79510328--fa8ae3b0eaaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/taiwan-first-new-f-16v-fighters-arrive-amid-china-threat/a-79510328?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US-made jets, part of an order made in 2019, touched down as concerns grow in Taiwan that support from the United States could be wavering. Washington insists its policy towards Taiwan and China hasn't changed.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
